General registration is open on selinuxnews.org.

This means you can register an account to post comments or author news 
articles.

If you are an SELinux developer or otherwise involved in the project, 
please consider registering and posting brief news articles whenever you 
do or find something worth noting.

The idea is that this site is a central repository of news & information 
relating to SELinux, so that people can keep up with everything that's 
been going on.


For authors:
------------
Once registered, I will upgrade you to an author if I know who you are.
Otherwise, if you want to post articles, get someone I know to vouch for 
you or just email me the article and I'll post it.

New features or notable changes, media coverage, presentation materials, 
deployments, events etc. are all good topics.


Before posting, please read the Author Guide:
